## Control {{controlId}}: Deny Network Communications Traffic by Default and Allow by Exception

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization implements a deny-all, permit-by-exception network communications posture within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through Conditional Access policies and named location restrictions managed by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if conditionalAccessActive}}
**Default-Deny Policy Enforcement:**
{{caPoliciesTotalCount}} Conditional Access policies implement default-deny controls, requiring explicit authorization for all network communications:
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{state}}): Applied to {{conditions.users}} users across {{conditions.applications}} applications. Requires {{#each grantControls.builtInControls}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}.
{{/each}}
{{else}}
Conditional Access default-deny policies have not been configured. Network communications are permitted without explicit authorization controls.
{{/if}}

{{#if namedLocationsConfigured}}
**Location-Based Exceptions:**
Network access is restricted to {{namedLocationsCount}} authorized locations. Traffic originating from unrecognized locations is blocked by default:
{{#each locations}}
- **{{displayName}}**{{#if isTrusted}} (Trusted){{/if}}{{#if ipRanges}} — {{#each ipRanges}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}{{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{else}}
Named locations have not been defined. Location-based deny-by-default enforcement is not active.
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine Conditional Access policy configurations, named location definitions, default block rules, and exception authorization documentation.

